    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 39 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`, including every duplicate-detection checkpoint (Cp03, Cp10, Cp11, Cp25, and the new Cp28).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Removed the three separate `rejectDuplicateTelephone`, `rejectDuplicateEmail`, and `rejectDuplicateHousehold` checks. Replaced them with a single `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner)` that computes the owner's whole `identityKey` and rejects with 409 only when it exactly equals an existing owner's. The `sharesHousehold` branch now only assigns the `householdId` (via the existing `assignHousehold`); the identity check then runs afterward so the compared key reflects the assigned household. Added a shared `identityKey(Owner)` helper.\n\n2. **`DuplicateIdentityException.java`** \u2014 New exception carrying the conflicting key; deleted the three old `Duplicate{Telephone,Email,Household}Exception` classes.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 Replaced the three old 409 handlers with one `handleDuplicateIdentityException` (still 409 Conflict, `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `identityKey` string property to the `Owner` schema, so it's returned by the API (DTO is generated at build time).\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Maps `identityKey` onto the DTO using the same derivation, so the returned value matches the key used for duplicate detection.\n\n**Behaviour change confirmed by the tests:** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different `identityKey`s and are both allowed (Cp11); only an exact full-key match is rejected (Cp03/Cp10/Cp25/Cp28).",
